  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) achieved 0.7207 accuracy, far surpassing all other configs. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200) was the dominant factor, but the image encoder dimension has not yet been explored with scvi_n200. All top configs used imagenet_vit_l, and the image-only baseline (config_013) was very low (0.2596), suggesting the image branch contributes differently depending on the encoder. Question: Does resnet50 complement scvi_n200 better than imagenet_vit_l, potentially yielding a higher accuracy? This is the most impactful unexplored axis for our best-performing RNA encoder. Why this experiment: With 4 experiments remaining, testing a new image encoder paired with the clearly superior scvi_n200 + transformer + concat stack offers the highest potential upside to beat 0.7207, while keeping all other variables (aggregation, fusion, profile) fixed at their best-known values. It reduces uncertainty about whether the current 0.7207 is near-optimal or whether a different visual backbone could push performance higher."
}

